\section{Conclusions}
\label{sec:conclusions}
\noindent
The HIghMass sample is a unique sample of several dozen unusually \HI-rich high mass galaxies out of galaxies detected in ALFALFA with \HI\ masses $>10^{10}$ M$_\odot$. In this paper, we have presented a first look at two of these galaxies using high-resolution VLA observations combined with previous \Halpha\ and optical imaging. We have derived structural and dynamical parameters of the gas distribution and derived dark matter halo properties, including their spin parameters. Future analysis will extend these techniques to the rest of the HIghMass sample.

